<section id="time-control">
  <h2>5. Time Control Patterns and Game Characteristics</h2>

  <p class="text-block">
    The dataset spans <strong>175 unique time control configurations</strong>. The dominant format is
    <strong>10+0 (blitz, no increment)</strong> at 7,721 games (38.5% of the dataset), followed by 15+0 rapid (1,311)
    and 15+15 (850). Time controls shape not only game length but also <em>how</em> games end &mdash; with faster
    controls producing more timeouts and fewer checkmates.
  </p>

  <div class="chart-row">
    <div class="chart-box">
